{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-117610",
    "CVE-2026-113351",
    "CVE-2026-124317",
    "CVE-2026-77214",
    "CVE-2026-134703",
    "CVE-2026-115506",
    "CVE-2026-102633",
    "CVE-2026-128241",
    "CVE-2026-93990",
    "CVE-2026-118370"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that Expat did not properly validate UTF-16 surrogate\npairs. An attacker could possibly use this issue to pass malformed\ncharacters to applications using Expat, resulting in unexpected behavior.\n(CVE-2026-93990)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly computed memory allocation sizes\non 32-bit platforms, leading to an integer overflow. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause Expat to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice, or possibly execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-102633)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat did not properly validate buffer lengths under\ncertain circumstances, leading to a heap buffer over-read. An attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause Expat to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service, or obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-77214)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat detected certain entity expansion attacks too\nlate. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Expat to consume\nexcessive resources, leading to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-115506)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly tracked memory allocations when a\nparser was reset. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause later\ndocuments parsed with the same parser to fail, resulting in a denial of\nservice. This issue only affected Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-113351)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly handled a very large number of\nattributes, leading to an integer overflow. An attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause Expat to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or\npossibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-118370)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly handled empty input to external\nentity parsers, leading to a NULL pointer dereference. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause Expat to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-117610)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat incorrectly handled truncated multibyte\nsequences in documents with unknown encodings, leading to an out-of-bounds\nread. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Expat to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service, or obtain sensitive information.\n(CVE-2026-124317)\n\nIt was discovered that the xmlwf tool in Expat followed symbolic links when\nwriting output files with the -d option. A local attacker could possibly\nuse this issue to overwrite files with the privileges of the user running\nxmlwf. This update also changes xmlwf to create these output files with\n0600 permissions. (CVE-2026-128241)\n\nIt was discovered that Expat could split UTF-16 surrogate pairs when\nconverting UTF-16 input in non-native byte order. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to pass malformed characters to applications using\nExpat, resulting in unexpected behavior. (CVE-2026-134703)",
  "id": "USN-9196-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in Expat.",
